## Verdict

**approve with changes.**

Blocker 1 is closed the way the fix prompt specified and survives the adversarial routes it did not name (`.pth`/user-site injection, a `.pth` pointing at a full checkout, symlinks out of the tree, a symlinked repo path), while exp_03's 12-file closure and digest `5ba818d8…` are reproduced exactly at `62c9107`. Findings 2–5 and nits 6–11 are closed as specified, each with a test; the launcher now refuses every output-side and input-side tamper I could construct with stub children and finalises only a directory containing exactly the three files; the 32-query K = 8 parity holds bit for bit through the fixed launcher on GPU 1 (frozen evaluator = launcher PE, and the P run's P section identical), with the `--gpu`, `--bind-input`, 40-hex resolution and the bounded-run dirty gate all exercised on the real path; the suite is effectively 559 green. What remains is small and non-blocking: the dirty gate's smoke/confirmatory boundary lets a `--max-samples ≥ split` full-split run through as a smoke (1), the console mirror can overwrite the launcher's own lines under `2> file` (2, already fixed on the training side in `07f3bc9`), and the abort path can rename a log it did not create (3); the training launcher should get the same log rename and `required=` set (4, round-3b's file).

