codex
Implemented in 14 commits, all under 200 changed lines with the required trailer. No push, history rewrite, full training run, or edits to protected files.

The full suite ran once: **702 passed, 3 failed**. All three host-specific recovery failures were corrected afterward; **102 affected tests then passed**. Compilation and shell checks pass. Unrestricted whitespace checking flags only the existing worklog transcript.

| Commit | Changed lines | Focused tests passed |
|---|---:|---:|
| `9b47c7a` | 75 | 61 |
| `5d04d0a` | 115 | 69 |
| `8a8e515` | 138 | 76 |
| `b48cd7b` | 70 | 110 |
| `5d6d4f9` | 51 | 83 |
| `248688b` | 99 | 84 |
| `f518224` | 127 | 123 |
| `32c3df5` | 66 | 133; 1 failed |
| `7306ff6` | 1 | 134 |
| `90a6077` | 61 | 127 |
| `4772e15` | 31 | 97 |
| `89521df` | 21 | 99 |
| `30779cb` | 121 | 106 |
| `f7596c0` | 48 | 102 |

Discrepancies and limits:

- The four groups were subdivided for commit size. `32c3df5` was committed before noticing its fixture failure; `7306ff6` corrected it.
- Recovery requires recorded execution evidence. Its `fuser` check cannot inspect inaccessible users’ descriptors.
- Protected producer code still does not enforce the new evaluation flags/binding names. Round-3a nits 7–9 remain unchanged.

[Full SHAs, validation details, and limitations](/tmp/exp04_round3b_closeout_report.md) · [Full-suite log](/tmp/exp04_round3b_closeout_full_suite.log)
